# Content pipeline — stage mapping

See `PROJECT.md` §2 for the full table.

## Stage 1 (current) — do this

- **4** Image/infographic **placeholders** only (no real image APIs)
- **5** `title`, `meta_description`, `url_slug` — prompt rules + persisted fields
- **10** Callouts: Совет / Важно / Подсказка / Лайфхак / Рекомендация (prompt; only where natural)
- Basic generation from brief / `outline` (manual outline in `topics.json` is OK)

## After competitor analysis (Stage 3) — not now

- **1** TOP competitor articles
- **2** Competitor structure → improved outline
- **3** Generate article **from that** competitor-based structure

## Later

| # | Feature | Stage |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 6 | Dzen shorter unique article | 1.1 / 9 |
| 7 | Internal linking | 6 |
| 4 real images | Image generation/search | 6 |
| 8 | Detectors + optional Humanizer API | 9 |
| 9 | Optimization + summary | 9 |

## Do not

- Pull SERP/competitors, Humanizer SaaS, detectors, or CMS into Stage 1 without an explicit assignment.
- Replace Markdown storage with HTML-only or image-only flows.
